-3.  **Compute Probabilistic Distribution:** Compute the cumulative distribution or histogram of the values in $R_i$ to determine the statistical distribution of residuals [S1].
-4.  **Identify Corrupt Pixels:** Determine the threshold value corresponding to the $(1-\alpha)$-quantile of the residual distribution [S1]. Pixels with residuals greater than or equal to this threshold are identified as corrupt [S1]. Specifically, locate pixels with the last $\alpha$-quantile residuals (largest residuals) [S1].
-5.  **Patch Depth:** Replace the depth values at the identified corrupt pixel locations in the input depth map $D_i$ with the corresponding values from the underfitting depth map $D_b^K_i$ [S1].
-6.  **Resume Optimization:** Use $D_{patched}$ for depth supervision in subsequent training iterations [S1].
+*   $K$: The number of training iterations after which the underfitting depth is sampled. Typical value: 4000 [S1].
+*   $\alpha$: The fraction of pixels with the largest residuals to patch. Typical value: 0.1 [S1].
 
